./ ALIAS NAME=PE                                                                
)F FUNCTION -                                                                   
  The PERMIT command grants acces to a resource in a certain class.             
  It writes one line in the PROFILES member of SYS1.SECURE.CNTL.                
                                                                                
  PERMIT updates the control data sets on disk only.  Reload the in             
  core tables afterwards with 'S RAKFPROF' from the console, or by              
  running the RAKFPROF procedure in batch, or the profile is not in             
  effect.                                                                       
                                                                                
  You must be connected to the RAKFADM group. PERMIT is an ordinary             
  problem state program - it is the protection on the control data sets         
  that enforces this, not APF authorization.                                    
                                                                                
  NOTE - a profile record with UACC (the universal access record)               
         must exist, otherwise the PERMIT fails.                                
         Universal access records are created by ADDSD and RRDEFINE.            
                                                                                
)X SYNTAX -                                                                     
  PERMIT 'resource' CLASS(clasname) ACCESS(NONE/READ/UPDATE/ALTER) +            
         ID(group)                                                              
                                                                                
  ALIAS: PE                                                                     
                                                                                
  REQUIRED - 'resource'                                                         
             ID(group)                                                          
                                                                                
  DEFAULT  - ACCESS(NONE)                                                       
             CLASS(DATASET)                                                     
                                                                                
  EXAMPLE  - PERMIT $TSTVS.* CLASS(FACILITY) ID(ADMIN) ACCESS(READ)             
                                                                                
  OR         PERMIT SYS1.LINKLIB ID(ADMIN) ACCESS(READ)                         
                                                                                
  The operands can be shortened to the shortest unique abbreviation.            
  So, PE $TSTVS.* C(FACILITY) I(ADMIN) A(READ)                                  
  is also valid.                                                                
                                                                                
  RETURN CODES:                                                                 
                                                                                
     0 - The resource is created.                                               
     8 - An error occurs. A suitable message will be given to                   
         the user.                                                              
)O OPERANDS -                                                                   
))'resource' - the generalized resource in the specified class. The             
  length can be up to 44 bytes. Generic resources can be created.               
))CLASS - Specify the name of the generalized resource class. The               
  class name is alphabetic value with a length up to 8 characters.              
  Default = CLASS(DATASET).                                                     
))ID    - Specify the name of the group that grants access. The                 
  group name is alphabetic value with a length up to 8 characters.              
))ACCESS - Specify the to be granted access of the resource.                    
  possible values are: NONE (no access), READ, UPDATE and                       
  ALTER (delete and create). Default = NONE.                                    
